      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "FRQ · Parametric motion",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A curve is given by \\( x(t)=t^2 \\), \\( y(t)=t^3-3t \\). Find the slope \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} \\) at \\( t=2 \\). <p>Differentiate each: \\( \\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t \\), \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2-3 \\). Then</p>\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3t^2-3}{2t}\\Big|_{t=2}=\\frac{12-3}{4}=\\frac{9}{4}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "FRQ · Interval of convergence",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the interval of convergence of \\( \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{x^n}{n} \\). <p>Ratio test: \\( \\left|\\dfrac{x^{n+1}/(n+1)}{x^n/n}\\right|=|x|\\cdot\\dfrac{n}{n+1}\\to|x| \\), so it converges for \\( |x|&lt;1 \\). Check endpoints: \\( x=1 \\) gives the divergent harmonic series; \\( x=-1 \\) gives the convergent alternating harmonic series.</p>\\[ \\text{Interval of convergence: } [-1,\\,1). \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
